.TH WREX-ETH 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-eth \- eth layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIeth\fR \fB--eth\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIeth\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Ethernet II (DIX) framing: 14\-byte header (destination MAC, source MAC, EtherType). Valid stack start (rank 10). EtherType drives the chain: 0x0800 \-> ipv4, 0x0806 \-> arp, 0x86dd \-> ipv6, 0x8100/0x88a8 \-> vlan, anything else \-> synthesized `unknown` layer holding the remaining bytes.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 10 (valid stack start: no parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --eth-dst).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-eth\-dst=\fIMAC\fR\fR
destination MAC (autofill: ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff) Type mac. Default: ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff.
.TP
\fB\-\-eth\-src=\fIMAC\fR\fR
source MAC (autofill: interface MAC on send) Type mac. Default: 00:00:00:00:00:00.
.TP
\fB\-\-eth\-type=\fIINT\fR\fR
ethertype (autofill: derived from next layer) Type u16. Default: 0.

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \\\\
  \-\-eth\-dst=ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff \-\-eth\-type=0x0800
wrex fields eth

